    "content": "As of mid-March 2026, SpaceX maintains a high-tempo launch schedule, heavily dominated by weekly Falcon 9 Starlink missions from Florida and California, with over 30 launches completed early in the year. Major upcoming missions include the Artemis II lunar mission (targeted for April 2026) and continued Starship testing. Upcoming SpaceX Launches (March 2026 & Beyond) March 16, 2026: Starlink Mission - Falcon 9 (Cape Canaveral SFS) March 18, 2026: Starlink Mission - Falcon 9 (Cape Canaveral SFS) April 2026: Artemis II Crewed Lunar Mission - Falcon Heavy (NASA) (NET April 6) April 2026: ViaSat-3 F3 - Falcon Heavy (Kennedy Space Center) May 2026: MRV-1 Mission (Cape Canaveral) June 2026: SDA Tranche 1 Tracking Layer (Vandenberg SFB) July 2026: Griffin Mission One - Falcon Heavy (Kennedy Space Center) Key 2026 Mission Highlights Starlink: Frequent, weekly launches continuing throughout the year to build the Gen2 constellation. Artemis II: NASA's first crewed mission to the Moon in over 50 years, using a SpaceX Falcon Heavy for training and validation, with a critical window in April. Starship: Continued rapid development testing and, likely, further orbital flight tests from Starbase, Texas, following 2025 flights. Commercial/Gov: Future launches for 2026 include the Nancy Grace Roman Space Telescope (September). All launch dates are subject to change due to weather or technical constraints.",
